+ 4. Charge: 12.0 V on the DC inlet, the pack connected with its SMBus. The charger delivers into the pack the current the panel controller programmed, and the pack's gauge (BQ4050) opens its own charge FET when its cell-surface thermistor reads outside 0 to 45 C (`pcb_pack_protection.yaml` CHARGE_TEMPERATURE_WINDOW). **Corrected 26 September 2026:** the step read as if the charger saw the thermistor, and the BQ25731 has no thermistor input (TI SLUSE66A, Table 7-1). Since `faf8c981` and `458b2873` the charger's cell-count strap selects 4S and the SMBus lead mates (`PANEL.md` section 10, section 4 above); the kit's loads sit on the charger's system side, so read the pack's own current at the gauge rather than the charger's input current (corrected 26 September 2026, S-07: this step said it could not pass).
+ 5. The stack with B16: each module boots from its rail with the other two slots disabled, then all three together; every USB device enumerates on its hub; the Ethernet switch links all three and the wall port. Record each rail's current at idle and with the display on.
+ 6. Bursts: 5G registration, one Iridium session, one LoRa transmission and one VHF key-down in turn, each rail watched at its connector, then all within the same second: what is being recorded is the margin.
+-7. Panel: the panel controller enumerates; lamp test lights all 17 LEDs; BLACKOUT kills the rail; the EMCON toggle locked closed keeps the SA868 and the PA in receive while the bridge asserts PTT and opens every transmitter rail gate, and every other radio goes dark (D-05, `PANEL.md` section 6), measured with an external receiver; ZEROIZE armed shows on the e-paper and, held 5 s, performs the erase of `PANEL.md` section 6 (decision 30: the secure element's wrapping key destroyed, the running modules' RAM keys dropped, the slots cut), after which no drive unlocks; SOS closed 2 s under EMCON queues its message and tells the operator (D-10, `PANEL.md` section 9).
++7. Panel: the panel controller enumerates; lamp test lights all seventeen controller-lit indicators (the sixteen panel LEDs `D1` to `D16`, the TX lamp `D3` among them through its tie `D17`, and the PI button's ring; `PANEL.md` section 9); BLACKOUT kills the rail; the EMCON toggle locked closed keeps the SA868 and the PA in receive while the bridge asserts PTT and opens every transmitter rail gate, and every other radio goes dark (D-05, `PANEL.md` section 6), measured with an external receiver; ZEROIZE armed shows on the e-paper and, held 5 s, performs the erase of `PANEL.md` section 6 (decision 30: the secure element's wrapping key destroyed, the running modules' RAM keys dropped, the slots cut), after which no drive unlocks; SOS closed 2 s under EMCON queues its message and tells the operator (D-10, `PANEL.md` section 9).
+ 8. Power loss: pull the DC lead and confirm the kit keeps running from the pack and the panel shows SHORE off.
+ 9. Shore inhibit: `SHORE_INHIBIT` high holds the front end off within a second, low restores it.
+-10. PA: 10 minutes of key-down at 30 W into a load; the plate temperature at the flange and the case skin temperature recorded, the fans running.
++10. PA: key-downs of at most 60 s each at 30 W into a load, at least 2 s apart, each started only inside K2 and ended by C4 (`feasibility/POWER-THERMAL.md` sections 7.2 and 9.3), as `TEST-PLAN.md` T-H3 runs them; the flange sensor and a thermocouple beside it logged, and the case skin temperature recorded, the fans running. **Corrected 27 September 2026 (Review A of layer 2, finding B6; `CONOPS.md` section 4d):** this step was ten minutes of key-down at 30 W, which K1 forbids: one 60 s key-down at 45 W of heat from a +50 C plate already puts the flange at about 95 C on the record's own figure, against the RA30H1317M1's +100 C case maximum and its 90 C advice (PWR-F15).
+ 11. Blind-mate: lift the stack and set it back three times, each time by the procedure of section 7 (kit off, outside leads and pack unplugged, the cap on E5 while it is out). Every RF path still passes, the pre-charge pin still mates first, and nothing on the block is scored.
+ 12. Pack gauge data flash (decision 40, owner ruling of 26 September 2026), before the pack is first charged or discharged: read the BQ4050's protection thresholds and enabled protections back and compare them with `pcb_pack_protection.yaml`. Board P's second level covers cell under-voltage in hardware since `faf8c981` (D-15's first branch), so the read-back is the check D-15 keeps; only after it passes is the chemical fuse armed by closing `JP1` (`gen_sch_p.py` docstring and `:476`; corrected 26 September 2026, S-07).
