 ## 4. Functional check (run before and after every test)
 
 Power on from the pack; the panel controller reports; every bearer comes up and passes traffic (Iridium message, 5G data, WiFi link to a second kit or a laptop, LoRa mesh packet, Zigbee and Thread join, APRS beacon heard by a receiver, HF CAT and audio, SDR capture, GNSS fix with time pulse); the display, touch, e-paper, LEDs, sounder, headset audio and PTT, camera; the sensors report; the seal check (inside against outside pressure after the valve settles) passes; EMCON silences every transmitter, measured with a receiver or spectrum analyser outside the kit and never with the kit's own SDR, whose supply EMCON removes (the per-transmitter bench tests of `feasibility/EMCON.md` section 6; corrected 26 September 2026, S-07); blackout darkens the kit; ZEROIZE wipes the secure element (verified by a failed key operation afterwards); the tamper switch logs the lid; shore, solar and vehicle inputs charge the pack; the PoE and USB-C outlets deliver; the log holds every step.
 
+**Purpose and trace.** Acceptance, run before and after every test and at commissioning (`CONOPS.md` section 4d). It verifies: the core bearers passing traffic, REQ-001; the other bearers, REQ-002; a message each way over each long-range bearer in turn, with the kit's own hand-off within 10 s and the end-to-end time recorded as characterisation, REQ-003 (`CONOPS.md` section 4c); with one long-range bearer disabled, its queue delivered over the next bearer within 10 s of the bearer being declared down (NEED-02; the requirement record is the registry writer's); the face, the e-paper and the indicators, REQ-007, REQ-008, REQ-013; the TX lamp and its lamp-test tie, REQ-012; the headsets, REQ-009; the camera, REQ-010; the sensors, REQ-041; the seal check, REQ-021 and CON-008; EMCON with its latency per row and the EMCON lamp once it is drawn, REQ-030, REQ-031, REQ-032 (the bench tests E-01 to E-12 of `feasibility/EMCON.md` section 6 carry the fault conditions); blackout, REQ-033; ZEROIZE and its indications, REQ-035 and REQ-038 (the drives re-enrolled afterwards); the tamper switch and the lid-driven reduced mode, entered also after a start with the lid closed once the lid is read, REQ-036 and REQ-052; SOS, its queue under EMCON and its indications, REQ-060; the slot supervision, REQ-062; charging from each input, REQ-015, REQ-016, REQ-046; the outlets and their interlock, REQ-017 and CON-019. The failover fabric is accepted by `ARCH-PCB-B-IOHA.md` section 13's tests A1 to A14, each device of a moved bank back in service (`ARCH-PCB-B-IOHA.md` section 7 step 12, application access resumed) within 30 s plus its maker's start-up, and the bridge's own service back on a surviving module within 60 s of the loss (REQ-004, `CONOPS.md` section 4c).
